{%- comment -%}
  Single source of truth for the eBay social-proof claim.

  Verified 21 Aug 2026 on the seller profile: inature, 100% positive Feedback
  (157). Of that score, eBay's own page reports "eBay automated feedback: 136"
  and 46 results under the "Feedback left by buyer" filter. So 157 is a count of
  positive transactions, NOT a count of written reviews. The previous wording,
  "140 verified eBay reviews", counted eBay's automated entries as reviews.

  Under the DMCC Act 2024 that distinction matters, so the two numbers are kept
  apart here and every page pulls the wording from this one snippet.

  Usage:
    {% render 'social-proof-line' %}            100% positive eBay feedback across 157 orders
    {% render 'social-proof-line', style: 'reviews' %}   46 verified buyer reviews on eBay
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign ebay_feedback_score = 157 -%}
{%- assign ebay_written_reviews = 46 -%}

{%- case style -%}
  {%- when 'reviews' -%}
    {{ ebay_written_reviews }} verified buyer reviews on eBay
  {%- else -%}
    100% positive eBay feedback across {{ ebay_feedback_score }} orders
{%- endcase -%}
